From 9ec7ff9280603acda5c63311fdedce42ea188873 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:37:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/16] call-host: child workdirs unique by construction;
 experiment-side follow-ups to patches 06-08

- call-host served several solver runs (each check case) whose child spans repeat, so
  concurrent cases shared a workdir (the F1 hazard) and the new lock refused two of them;
  calls/, interpret/ and agents/ workdirs now carry a host tag and a sequence number (the
  plan's 'unique workdirs by construction'); the lock stays as the guard.
- jit/stats.mjs ENV_FAULT_CODES follows runner.mjs ENV_FAULTS (patch 06, WORKDIR_BUSY), as
  its test requires.
- slice2-wiring: the flow-v3 pin moves with patch 07 (the old bytes are SOP-Bench p2's
  frozen SDK copy, unchanged); the host check's three identical leaf calls are now one
  joined call (patch 08 single flight), so it pays one judge, not three.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011geBy7JvDqKuqhDyfmzd1U
